{{Documentation}}
Module to display the stats of an enemy at the magnification specified, for use in the infoboxes [[Template:Stage Info|Stage]] and [[Template:Story Info|Story Info]].

==How to use==
#Write out the name of the first enemy (see [[Module:Enemies/data/doc|here]]) for a list if you get [[:Category:Pages with script errors|script errors]]), then its magnification (doesn't matter if it has commas or % signs; these are preferred for code aesthetics)
#Do this for each other enemy
#This then outputs a formatted enemy list like in the example given. Make sure to use the preview option if you're inexperienced with this template.

==Example Usage==
<pre>
{{Magnification
|Doge|1000
|Doge|1,000
|Doge|1000%
|Doge|1,000%
|Pigge|100%
|Sho Ayanokoji|100/100%
|High Priest Mamon|0
|Swordsman (form 1)|980%
|Codename "Red Riding"|22%
}}
</pre>
gives<br>
{{Magnification
|Doge|1000
|Doge|1,000
|Doge|1000%
|Doge|1,000%
|Pigge|100%
|Sho Ayanokoji|100/100%
|High Priest Mamon|0
|Swordsman (form 1)|980%
|Codename "Red Riding"|22%
}}

==Additional notes==
*If you specify two values separated by a /, such as in the Ayanokōji Shō example above, you can specify when an enemy has separate HP and attack magnifications
*If you set the magnification to 0, as in the High Priest Mamon example, no magnification is stated. This behaviour can be used to format [[Catclaw Dojo]] and [[Gauntlet]] stages where due to technical issues on FANDOM's side newlines cause formatting inconsistencies within infoboxes and tables.